claim.claim-text:
20. A system for vertically stabilizing objects, comprising:
a bipedal robot positioned on a support surface in an upright state;
a motion system for moving the bipedal robot on the support surface with omnidirectional movements;
a sensor assembly monitoring the bipedal robot; and
a controller with a processor running a stabilizing module to process data from the sensor assembly to determine when the bipedal robot is tipping away from the upright state and, in response, to generate control signals to operate the motion system to move at least one lower contact surface of the bipedal robot contacting the support surface to counter the tipping away.
